Aether: fingerprinting core

RFP off by default, signal registry, canvas/WebGL/audio noise, core count, text metrics, master switch, audiobuffer noise, per-site exceptions, UA compat token, worker cores.

Squashed from 13 units:

  [core/109-disable-rfp-by-default.patch]
  Aether: disable resistFingerprinting by default (keep code as fallback)
  
  Keep the RFP code in the tree but stop applying it: our own graded
  anti-fingerprinting system replaces it piece by piece, and RFP's
  normalize-everything policy would mask those experiments (and keeps
  breaking sites in the meantime). The policy code stays untouched as a
  reversible fallback; only the default flips. Until our layers land the
  browser identifies more easily than with RFP on: accepted interim cost,
  supersedes the old do-not-touch-RFP rule.
  
  [core/110-fingerprinting-signal-registry.patch]
  Aether: commit the fingerprinting signal registry
  
  Commit the fingerprinting signal registry that the from-scratch graded
  system will implement against: every script-readable surface with its
  verified implementation location, the RFP behavior documented for
  delimitation only, the assigned Aether policy (normalize/noise/restrict/
  leave), the level it belongs to, and the gate that proves it. Decisions
  already taken are pinned in _meta (third-party priority, real TZ/locale
  in Standard, per-launch seed, local-only diagnostics, noise at read
  time). Absent surfaces (deviceMemory, Client Hints) are recorded so
  nobody hunts them later. New directory without moz.build, so the build
  ignores it; later patches implement P1 canvas noise against this contract.
  
  [core/111-canvas-noise-2d-reads.patch]
  Aether: deterministic per-site noise on 2D canvas reads
  
  First graded layer built from zero: deterministic per-site noise on 2D
  canvas reads. A new dom/canvas module (own session secret per launch,
  SHA-256 stretched per first-party base domain, SplitMix64 pixel stream)
  flips the blue LSB of pixel 0 plus ~1/256 of the rest, at read time only:
  same site+session reads identical pixels, another site reads different
  ones, relaunch reseeds. Hooked into the single GetImageDataArray seam all
  2D reads flow through (display path untouched); services run before the
  cannot-GC region, the pixel pass is pure integer math. Kill pref
  aether.fingerprinting.canvasNoise2d, default on. Encode paths
  (toDataURL/toBlob) and WebGL/audio follow in later units. Gate: harness
  proves same-origin reread identical, cross-origin different, pref-off
  identical everywhere, plus CreepJS zero lies by the user.
  
  [core/112-canvas-noise-encode-paths.patch]
  Aether: per-site noise on canvas encode reads
  
  Extend the P1b encode-path noise (toDataURL/toBlob share the owned
  packed-BGRA copy in GetImageBuffer) with the same per-site key: blue LSB
  via the new channel-offset parameter, display never touched. Harness now
  digests all three read methods on both origins. Gate: every method stable
  per site+session and differing per site with noise on; all identical with
  the kill pref off.
  
  [core/113-webgl-noise-reads.patch]
  Aether: per-site WebGL renderer strings and readback noise
  
  P2 WebGL, from zero: coherent per-site renderer/vendor triples plus
  readPixels noise. A curated table of 8 Windows-plausible (vendor,
  unmasked, masked) triples feeds masked RENDERER, UNMASKED RENDERER and
  UNMASKED VENDOR from one per-site pick, so the three can never contradict
  each other; masked VENDOR stays stock ("Mozilla"). RGBA8 readPixels goes
  through the same keyed blue-LSB pass on the caller array. Shared module
  gains the pref-parameterized key helper and SelectIndex; new webglNoise
  kill pref default on. Gate: renderer strings + readPixels stable per
  site+session, differing per site, masked/unmasked coherent.
  
  [core/114-webaudio-analyser-noise.patch]
  Aether: per-site noise on WebAudio Analyser readouts
  
  P2 WebAudio, from zero: deterministic per-site noise on AnalyserNode
  readouts (float/bit frequency + time domain), keyed like canvas/WebGL with
  its own audioNoise kill pref. Noise lands on caller-owned arrays only, pure
  math inside the cannot-GC region, never on the audio path. AudioBuffer
  getChannelData is explicitly deferred: it returns the live shared buffer,
  so read-time noise would accumulate across reads (unstable, audible); that
  needs render-time keying in a later unit. Shared module gains KeyForAudio
  and ApplyNoiseFloat. Gate: analyser digests stable per site+session and
  differing per site, all three canvas methods + WebGL still green.
  
  [core/115-normalize-hardware-concurrency.patch]
  Aether: report the common core count
  
  Layer A begins: report the common desktop core count (8) instead of the
  real one, behind its own kill pref default on. One seam in
  Navigator::HardwareConcurrency; internal pool sizing is unaffected in any
  breaking direction. Harness now also asserts navigator props on both
  origins. Gate: 8 everywhere with the pref on, real identical count with
  it off, all previous gates still green.
  
  [core/116-canvas-text-metrics-nudge.patch]
  Aether: keyed one-ulp nudge on canvas measureText
  
  Canvas text metrics: nudge the reported measureText width by exactly one
  ulp, up or down per a stream keyed by site and the measured text itself.
  Same text reads back identically per site+session; other sites pick their
  own direction; drawing never sees it (measure branch returns before any
  painting). Shared module gains KeyForText, FNV-1a context mixing and
  NudgeDouble; new textMetrics kill pref default on. Harness digests five
  font-stack widths on both origins. Gate: stable + cross-differing with
  noise on, identical with it off, all previous gates still green.
  
  [core/117-fingerprinting-master-switch.patch]
  Aether: master kill-switch for the fingerprinting system
  
  Master kill-switch for the whole graded system: one pref gates every
  surface (the shared key helper and the core-count normalization both
  check it first), with the per-surface kill prefs refining it. This is the
  backend the end-state UI will bind (master button + one toggle per
  surface). Default on. Gate: master-off run reads fully raw on every
  surface, identical to the all-prefs-off control.
  
  [core/118-audiobuffer-channel-noise.patch]
  Aether: key channel noise on first audio buffer extraction
  
  Close the getChannelData gap without touching the live reference: noise
  the stored channel samples at most once, on first extraction, keyed by the
  extracting reader's site (later readers stay stable; author rewrites via
  CopyToChannel clear the key). Detached (shared) storage is never mutated:
  CopyFromChannel noises only its outgoing copy, indexed by absolute sample
  position so it matches a full-buffer pass. Shared module gains the offset
  parameter on ApplyNoiseFloat. Gate: rendered-buffer digests stable per
  site+session and differing per site, analyser gates still green.
  
  [core/119-per-site-fingerprint-exceptions.patch]
  Aether: per-site fingerprinting exceptions backend
  
  Per-site exceptions backend (the broken-site switch will bind this):
  exact base-domain prefs exempt a surface or all surfaces on that site,
  checked synchronously from any thread (no sqlite, no async). The shared
  key helper takes the surface token; the core-count normalization checks
  its own exempt prefs via the document principal. Dynamic pref names need
  no defaults: absent means protected.
  
  Plus a correctness fix its own gate caught: the 8-entry renderer table
  collides pairwise with p=1/8 (observed live: identical unmasked strings
  on both origins), so triples are now generated parametrically
  (family x model x PCI ID from one keyed stream, ~800k combinations)
  keeping the exact sanitizer-output shape and vendor/renderer coherence.
  Gate: with canvas2d/text/cores exempted on one origin only, that origin
  reads byte-identical raw pixels (known baseline) and real cores while the
  other stays noised; unmasked renderer collision gone by construction.
  
  [core/120-firefox-ua-compat-token.patch]
  Aether: report the Firefox UA compat token
  
  Google serves its legacy basic-HTML page to unknown user agents, and ours
  carries no Firefox token (only Aether/156.0.1). Flip the upstream compat
  switch so both the HTTP User-Agent and navigator.userAgent include
  Firefox/156.0 alongside the honest Aether token. Side benefit: blending
  with the Firefox anonymity set instead of a unique Aether-only UA. Stays
  user-overridable. Gate: packaged default true, runtime UA contains the
  token, reporter confirms the modern Google page.
  
  [core/121-worker-hardware-concurrency.patch]
  Aether: common core count in workers
  
  Worker hardwareConcurrency leaked the real core count (caught live on
  CreepJS: window reported 8, workers 24): WorkerNavigator has its own
  HardwareConcurrency path. Same contract there, keyed by the worker
  principal, honoring master, kill and exempt prefs. Shared module gains
  the exported SiteExempted helper; both Navigator call sites use it
  instead of inline pref plumbing. Harness spawns a same-origin worker on
  both origins and asserts window/worker agreement. Gate: 8/8 everywhere
  with prefs on, real/agreeing with them off, exempt split respected.
